<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat bucks U.S. trend to trade down.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat bucks U.S. trend to trade down.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nearby most-active Sydney wheat futures bucked the trend to settle lower in light trading.</p>
<p>With six lots traded each, January and March settled A$2.50 and A$2.00 down.</p>
<p>Local grains traders said the market ignored a rise in most CBOT contracts overnight, reading the gains as temporary.</p>
<p>Sydney wheat futures have traded in &quot;roller-coaster fashion&quot; all week, trading in a range of about A$4.00, one noted.  </p>
